# HARD RULE — 6-Step Verification Pipeline (NON-NEGOTIABLE, ALL TASKS, ALWAYS)

Every single task — feature, balance tweak, visual, bug fix, rename, asset swap,
menu change, world change — MUST complete **all six steps below, in this order,
before it can be marked done.** No task is ever "verified" on fewer than six
screenshots: 3 isolated + 3 in-game, and BOTH before/after/compare pairs must
exist on disk and be read.

There are no exceptions. Not for "small" tasks. Not for renames. Not for "the
isolated test already exists". Not for "the in-game test is hard". Not for "I'm
confident it works." Confidence is not evidence. Screenshots are.

## THE 6 STEPS (exact order, all required)

### STEP 1 — ISOLATED "BEFORE"
- Capture the pre-change state in an ISOLATED context (dedicated
  `scenes/<x>_test/<x>_test.tscn` + `.gd`, self-contained: no main scene, no
  arena, no HUD, no world dependencies; the scene writes
  `user://selftest_report.json` and calls `get_tree().quit()`).
- If the change is ALREADY applied, TEMPORARILY REVERT it, capture the BEFORE
  isolated screenshot, then RE-APPLY the change. Never skip this by saying
  "the before state is obvious."
- Save as `tools/selftest/results/<feature>/iso_before_*.png`.

### STEP 2 — ISOLATED "AFTER"
- With the change applied, re-run the SAME isolated scene.
- Save as `tools/selftest/results/<feature>/iso_after_*.png`.

### STEP 3 — ISOLATED "COMPARE"
- Diff the isolated before vs after: run `tools/diff_screenshots.py` when
  available (pass `-BeforeShot` to `run_selftest.ps1`), or open BOTH images with
  the Read tool and state, in writing, the concrete pixel differences you see.
- **ALSO run `python tools/inspect_screenshot.py <screenshot.png>`** on each
  screenshot to get: content fill %, bounding box, position (CENTER/TOP-LEFT/etc),
  and a thumbnail with grid overlay. This catches bugs like "video stuck in
  top-left corner" that full-res screenshots miss. Read the thumbnail too.
- Save any `diff_*.png` / diff report + `thumb_*.png` next to the others.
- **Read all three** (iso_before, iso_after, diff) with the Read tool and
  reason about them. A passing report JSON alone is NOT a compare.

### STEP 4 — IN-GAME "BEFORE"
- In the REAL game (main scene / FFA / full world), capture the pre-change
  state the same way (dev command, selftest request, or temporary revert).
- Save as `tools/selftest/results/<feature>/ingame_before_*.png`.

### STEP 5 — IN-GAME "AFTER"
- With the change applied, capture the same in-game state.
- Save as `tools/selftest/results/<feature>/ingame_after_*.png`.

### STEP 6 — IN-GAME "COMPARE"
- Diff the in-game before vs after exactly as in Step 3.
- Run `python tools/inspect_screenshot.py` on both in-game screenshots.
- Read all three (ingame_before, ingame_after, diff) with the Read tool and
  state the visible delta.

## ORDER IS ENFORCED

- You may only start an IN-GAME step (4/5/6) AFTER the ISOLATED steps (1/2/3)
  have passed and their three screenshots have been read.
- "An in-game test already exists" does NOT count. Build / re-run the ISOLATED
  test FIRST, every time.
- If you are about to run an in-game test and have not done the isolated
  before/after/compare in THIS task's session, STOP and do the isolated steps.

## PER-TASK CHECKLIST (copy into your todos; ALL must be green)

```
- [ ] 1. Isolated BEFORE screenshot on disk + read
- [ ] 2. Isolated AFTER screenshot on disk + read
- [ ] 3. Isolated COMPARE (diff or side-by-side) done + read
- [ ] 4. In-game BEFORE screenshot on disk + read
- [ ] 5. In-game AFTER screenshot on disk + read
- [ ] 6. In-game COMPARE (diff or side-by-side) done + read
- [ ] 7. PLAN.md status updated, referencing all 6 screenshot paths
- [ ] 8. All 6+ screenshots + report JSONs committed to git and pushed
```

If ANY box is unchecked, the task is NOT done.

## IF A STATE CANNOT BE CAPTURED

If a before/after state genuinely cannot be produced (e.g. a one-time
first-launch behavior), state that explicitly in PLAN.md, capture the closest
possible proxy, and mark the task with a note that the specific pair was
impossible — never silently skip the step.

## WHEN A STEP FAILS

Fix the root cause, re-run that exact step, re-verify. Do not skip the failed
step. Do not mark the task done while any of the six is red. Keep the failing
evidence so progress is auditable.

## SCOPE

All tasks, every time. No task type is exempt.
